cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research data, please cite it as below."
title: "Graph Neural Networks for Ruby Code Generation: A Failed Experiment"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lawrenz"
    given-names: "Tim"
type: dataset
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/timlawrenz/jubilant-palm-tree"
keywords:
  - "graph neural networks"
  - "code generation"
  - "abstract syntax trees"
  - "negative results"
  - "research failure analysis"
  - "ruby programming"
  - "machine learning"
abstract: >
  This repository contains the complete experimental record of an attempt
  to use Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) for Ruby code generation through
  hierarchical AST decoding. The experiment demonstrates that while GNNs
  excel at code understanding tasks (26.6% improvement in complexity
  prediction), they fundamentally fail at code generation (0% syntactic
  validity) due to architectural mismatch with sequential programming
  languages. All data, models, training logs, and detailed failure
  analysis are preserved for the research community under CC0 license.
  
  Key finding: Code generation requires sequential/autoregressive models
  (transformers), not graph-based approaches. Complete documentation of
  this negative result is available to help future researchers avoid
  similar pitfalls.
date-released: 2025-11-26
